@meta
id: 23-02
title: Direction decides which word you get
chapter: 23
type: lesson
skills: complete-keyword
par: 69
minutes: 5
vscode: IntelliSense ranks candidates for you
open: order.provider.ts

@brief
`retryPayment` stops at a bare `return`. It should charge the card again:

    return this.paymentService.charge(order.id, order.total);

Two properties in this file start with `paymentS`: `paymentService`,
used a few lines above the cursor, and `paymentSchedule`, used a few
lines below. Completion finds them in a definite order, and the order
depends on which key you press. Get the right one without cycling.

@keys
| `Ctrl-N` | complete, scanning forward from the cursor |
| `Ctrl-P` | complete, scanning backward from the cursor |
| `Ctrl-N` / `Ctrl-P` in the menu | next / previous candidate |

@hints
`/return$` then `A this.paymentS`. Before pressing a completion key,
think about which of the two candidates is nearer in which direction.
--
`Ctrl-N` scans forward and finds `paymentSchedule` first, because it
is below the cursor. `Ctrl-P` scans backward and finds `paymentService`
first.
--
`A this.paymentS` `Ctrl-P` `.charge(order.id, order.total);` `Esc`.
Typing the dot accepts the candidate.

@solution
    /return$<Enter>
    A this.paymentS<Ctrl-P>.charge(order.id, order.total);<Esc>
    :wq<Enter>

`Ctrl-N` and `Ctrl-P` build the same candidate list; they differ only
in where they start. Forward from the cursor, the first hit is the
schedule; backward, it is the service. When the word you want is the
one you used most recently — which is most of the time, because code
is written top to bottom — `Ctrl-P` gets it in one press.

If you pressed `Ctrl-N` and got the wrong one, a second `Ctrl-N` moves
to the next candidate, and `Ctrl-P` moves back. That works, but it is
two extra keys and a glance at the menu. Choosing the direction is
free.

Notice what was not on the list: `PAYMENT_FAILED`. Completion matches
keyword characters, and an underscore after `PAYMENT` is not an `S`.

@start order.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';
import { PaymentSchedule } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.schedule';

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
    @inject(PaymentSchedule) protected paymentSchedule: PaymentSchedule,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(id: string) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return order;
  }

  public async cancel(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);
    const receipt = await this.paymentService.refund(order.id);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED', refundReceipt: receipt.id },
    });
  }

  public async retryPayment(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status !== 'PAYMENT_FAILED') {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_RETRYABLE');
    }

    return
  }

  public async schedulePayment(id: string, runAt: Date) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    return this.paymentSchedule.enqueue(order.id, runAt);
  }
}

@expected order.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';
import { PaymentSchedule } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.schedule';

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
    @inject(PaymentSchedule) protected paymentSchedule: PaymentSchedule,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(id: string) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return order;
  }

  public async cancel(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);
    const receipt = await this.paymentService.refund(order.id);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED', refundReceipt: receipt.id },
    });
  }

  public async retryPayment(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status !== 'PAYMENT_FAILED') {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_RETRYABLE');
    }

    return this.paymentService.charge(order.id, order.total);
  }

  public async schedulePayment(id: string, runAt: Date) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    return this.paymentSchedule.enqueue(order.id, runAt);
  }
}
